  "info": {
    "title": "auto-reel-ng API",
    "version": "1"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/healthz": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Healthz",
        "description": "Liveness + DB reachability (D-A6 open question, settled: yes).",
        "operationId": "healthz_healthz_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/events": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
        ],
        "summary": "Get Events",
        "description": "``GET /api/v1/events`` (task 2.2): every event, freshly scanned.\n\nBoth ways this read can fail are reported distinctly and in the shared problem\nshape: an unreachable job store as the 503 ``/healthz`` returns, a failed scan\nas the 502 the detail route already returns. Neither is retried and neither\ndegrades — ``list_events`` builds the complete list before returning, so a\nfailure part-way through yields an error, never a partial set.",
        "operationId": "get_events_api_v1_events_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EventSummaryOut"
                  },
                  "type": "array",
                  "title": "Response Get Events Api V1 Events Get"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/events/{event_id}/analysis": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
        ],
        "summary": "Get Analysis",
        "description": "``GET /api/v1/events/{event_id}/analysis`` (task 2.4): cached segments only.\n\nRegistered *before* the ``{event_id:path}`` detail route below: both patterns\nare greedy over ``/``, and Starlette matches routes in registration order, so\nthe more specific ``/analysis`` suffix must be tried first or the detail route\nwould swallow it (``event_id`` ending in literal ``/analysis``).",
        "operationId": "get_analysis_api_v1_events__event_id__analysis_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "event_id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Event Id"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnalysisOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/events/{event_id}/reel": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
        ],
        "summary": "Get Reel",
        "description": "``GET /api/v1/events/{event_id}/reel``: the editorial document as authored.\n\nThe exact inverse of the PUT below — same model, same serializer — so a client\nmay submit what it read without hand-building a write body. Registered *before*\nthe greedy ``{event_id:path}`` detail route for the reason the ``/analysis``\nroute documents. The response carries an ``ETag`` for the optional ``If-Match``\nprecondition on the write; there is deliberately no conditional GET (D-R4).",
        "operationId": "get_reel_api_v1_events__event_id__reel_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "event_id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Event Id"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EditorialDocumentBody-Output"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
        ],
        "summary": "Put Reel",
        "description": "``PUT /api/v1/events/{event_id}/reel``: apply a desired editorial state (D-E2).\n\nA coarse whole-document write: ``payload`` is the complete desired editorial\nstate, merged onto the event's existing structure (never replacing the file\noutright, D-E1) and validated fail-loud before anything is persisted. The\nroute carries no editorial logic of its own (D-E6) — it resolves the event,\ndelegates to the engine operation, and echoes the persisted document plus the\nevent's resulting staleness verdict (computed free, D-E5) so the client needs\nno follow-up GET. The write never enqueues and never touches the render\nmanifest.\n\nA successful write carries an ``ETag`` for the state it just persisted,\ncomputed from the returned document by the same helper ``get_reel`` uses, so a\nclient may chain conditional writes with no intervening read. A ``412`` carries\nnone: a client that lost the race must re-read before it overwrites.",
        "operationId": "put_reel_api_v1_events__event_id__reel_put",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "event_id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Event Id"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "If-Match",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "title": "If-Match"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EditorialDocumentBody-Input"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EditorialWriteResult"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/events/{event_id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "events"
