        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "identity",
          "status"
        ],
        "title": "ClipOut",
        "description": "One clip: identity, reconcile status, and the file facts a reorder view needs.\n\n``size`` (bytes) and ``mtime`` (timezone-aware UTC) come from the clip's own\ndirectory entry — **file** facts, never media facts. Nothing here is decoded or\nprobed, so the detail response stays probe-free (Principle IV); duration,\ndimensions and codec belong to the analysis cache, not this shape. Both are\n``None`` for a clip the document references but disk does not have: absence is\nreported, never fabricated as a zero or an epoch (Principle I)."
      },
